<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>

    <!--
      The theme for the module's two activities, and for nothing else — it is
      declared on each <activity> rather than on <application> so the media
      service (which draws no UI at all) keeps the platform default.

      AppCompat rather than the platform's DeviceDefault, and the reason is the
      settings screen: PreferenceFragmentCompat needs a FragmentActivity host
      and an AppCompat-derived theme to inflate against. Both activities then
      use the SAME base, because a module with two screens on two theming
      systems is a module where the next change has to ask which one it is in.

      DayNight because a head unit switches day/night on its own (lights, time
      of day) and a form that stays white at night is exactly the contrast
      problem VD-1 is about. NoActionBar because SDK 35 lays every window out
      edge-to-edge: the activities pad their own roots from a WindowInsets
      listener (AR-1), and an ActionBar would be the one piece of chrome outside
      the view they can reach.
    -->
    <style name="Theme.TomeSonic.Car" parent="Theme.AppCompat.DayNight.NoActionBar">
        <!-- Required by androidx.preference; without it PreferenceFragmentCompat
             falls back to its own default overlay, which is not derived from
             this theme. -->
        <item name="preferenceTheme">@style/PreferenceThemeOverlay</item>
    </style>
</resources>
